<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hiarbas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 81 BCE</span> · Also known as Iarbas of Numidia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hiarbas was a king of Numidia in the early first century BCE, installed after the expulsion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiempsal-ii">Hiempsal II</a> with the backing of the Marian faction in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>'s civil war. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulla">Sulla</a>'s lieutenant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompey">Pompey</a> invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> in 81 BCE, he defeated the Marian commander Gnaeus Domitius Ahenobarbus and his ally Hiarbas, who was captured and put to death, and Hiempsal II was restored.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hiarbas.jpg" alt="Hiarbas" width="320" height="278" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown, uploaded by Algérien Mzab · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hiarbas.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
